720	// ── DOCUMENT-STOP: no TF32 (float) A-transposed collective ───────────────
721	//  A `sm90_run_gemm_tf32_atb` (Sm90GemmAT<tfloat32_t>) was attempted and
722	//  REVERTED because CUTLASS 3.x fails a HARD static_assert for it:
723	//
724	//    sm90_mma_tma_gmma_rs_warpspecialized.hpp(193):
725	//      static assertion failed "SmemLayoutB K must be 128bytes to be transposed."
726	//
727	//  WHY: a ColumnMajor A operand routes Hopper through the RS (register-source)
728	//  warp-specialized mainloop, whose transposed-operand SMEM layout requires the
729	//  K tile to be 128 bytes wide. For tfloat32_t (4 B) with this 128x128x64 tile
730	//  that constraint is not satisfied, and there is no Auto schedule that relaxes
731	//  it for the TF32 RS path. (The half/bf16 AT path — Sm90GemmAT<half_t/
732	//  bfloat16_t> — DOES satisfy it and compiles, so sm90_run_gemm_atb<> above is
733	//  provided and live for those element types.)
734	//
735	//  CONSEQUENCE: the ViT wgrad (dW = dYᵀ·X, an inherently A-transposed GEMM —
736	//  the contraction index m is the leading/row dim of both row-major operands,
737	//  so one MUST be transposed and CUTLASS only supports the transposed operand
738	//  on B for TF32) uses the CUTLASS AT collective for half/bf16 and KEEPS the
739	//  scalar gemm_grad_weight_kernel fallback for float. `vit_run_gemm_atb<float>`
740	//  (vit_sm90.cuh) therefore returns cudaErrorNotSupported → scalar path.
741	
742	// FP16 in / FP32 acc / FP32 out, row-major A * row-major B, row-major C.
743	// Sm90 collective (TMA+WGMMA), FP32 accumulate — replaces the old Gemm<>
